Dialogue: 0,0:35:10.76,0:35:19.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,my good friend Mohamed Awad.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:19.08,0:35:20.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,Thanks, Matt.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:20.08,0:35:21.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,Thank you.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:21.08,0:35:22.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,Great seeing you, Charles.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:22.16,0:35:23.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,Thank you.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:23.68,0:35:27.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, Charles, before we let you go, we have one question for you.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:27.12,0:35:28.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,What's your question?
Dialogue: 0,0:35:28.84,0:35:33.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,Supermicro is known for speed to market and deployment velocity.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:33.44,0:35:39.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,Why is deployment speed becoming such a competitive advantage in AI infrastructure for Supermicro?
Dialogue: 0,0:35:39.68,0:35:40.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,Okay.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:41.00,0:35:47.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh infrastructure for agentic AI is all about time to first the token, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:35:47.48,0:35:56.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,And that's why uh we work with Arm uh to develop our building block solution for system level, for rack level, for data center level.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:56.56,0:36:03.30,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, with our building block solution, we see your technology, your CPU, your system architecture,
Dialogue: 0,0:36:03.35,0:36:11.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,we can quickly bring your solution, bring your CPU power to the market as soon as customer need.
Dialogue: 0,0:36:11.24,0:36:11.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,Absolutely.
Dialogue: 0,0:36:11.96,0:36:19.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, uh um the quicker our infrastructure get ready online, the quicker our customer can make money.
Dialogue: 0,0:36:19.20,0:36:21.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, that's why I'm very happy to work with you.
Dialogue: 0,0:36:21.76,0:36:22.32,Sub,,0,0,0,,Absolutely.
Dialogue: 0,0:36:22.37,0:36:22.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,Thank you.
Dialogue: 0,0:36:22.92,0:36:23.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,Thank you.
Dialogue: 0,0:36:23.48,0:36:24.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,Thank you.
Dialogue: 0,0:36:24.52,0:36:26.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,Thank you, Charles.
Dialogue: 0,0:36:26.48,0:36:26.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,Okay.
Dialogue: 0,0:36:26.96,0:36:27.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,Okay.
Dialogue: 0,0:36:27.44,0:36:37.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, Mohamed, I guess first question up, how is a gen AI changing the way our customers think about infrastructure compared to the last wave of gen AI?
Dialogue: 0,0:36:37.56,0:36:38.88,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah, I it's really wild.
Dialogue: 0,0:36:38.93,0:36:46.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,I mean the the the industry has kind of gone through this massive transformation over the last uh few years as as most of you know.
Dialogue: 0,0:36:46.80,0:36:51.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um you know, gen AI was all about users interacting with machines.
Dialogue: 0,0:36:51.88,0:36:57.04,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, a user is set up to a prompt, puts a request in, a bunch of tokens are generated,
Dialogue: 0,0:36:57.09,0:37:04.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,a CPU is there to kind of manage the the GPU or the accelerator, provide that response back to the user.
Dialogue: 0,0:37:04.76,0:37:08.49,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um and that was great, and we saw a boom in in sort of accelerators on the back of it.
Dialogue: 0,0:37:08.54,0:37:16.73,Sub,,0,0,0,,What we're seeing now with agentic is is it's kind of all shifting on its head where it's no longer about the user being the bottleneck.
Dialogue: 0,0:37:16.78,0:37:22.02,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's about, you know, CPUs responding directly.
Dialogue: 0,0:37:22.07,0:37:31.22,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, agents now taking over and actually responding to that those tokens that are being generated by the accelerator,
Dialogue: 0,0:37:31.27,0:37:35.61,Sub,,0,0,0,,and then maybe uh putting a bunch more requests into the accelerator.
Dialogue: 0,0:37:35.66,0:37:46.22,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, this kind of fluid flow of accelerators and and CPUs constantly communicating with each other, and then CPUs going off and generating more agents.
Dialogue: 0,0:37:46.27,0:37:50.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, you have agents generating agents, orchestrating additional agents.
Dialogue: 0,0:37:50.92,0:37:55.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,And here's the thing about the agents, unlike humans, they never sleep.
Dialogue: 0,0:37:55.92,0:37:57.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, there is no bottleneck anymore.
Dialogue: 0,0:37:57.28,0:38:06.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,There you have to respond at this kind of constant rate, and that's what's driving this massive influx and demand for more and more CPUs.
Dialogue: 0,0:38:06.12,0:38:12.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, on that topic, I mean, as you mentioned, orchestration is getting a heavier load, becoming more important.
Dialogue: 0,0:38:12.44,0:38:16.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, some people are saying the CPU is becoming relevant again.
Dialogue: 0,0:38:16.96,0:38:19.13,Sub,,0,0,0,,Well, I I think it was always relevant, so I don't know.
Dialogue: 0,0:38:19.18,0:38:21.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,As a CPU guy, I think it was always relevant.
Dialogue: 0,0:38:21.40,0:38:21.70,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:38:21.63,0:38:25.94,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah, no, I mean, I think I think what you're seeing is it's not like we we ever stopped using CPUs.
Dialogue: 0,0:38:25.99,0:38:32.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,They were always there managing the accelerators, managing the infrastructure, managing the storage, managing the networking.
Dialogue: 0,0:38:32.60,0:38:41.50,Sub,,0,0,0,,But, what you're seeing now is that as as CPUs start to become this this entity in and of itself that can go off and spawn workloads,
Dialogue: 0,0:38:41.55,0:38:46.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,or respond to workloads, they have to manage different uh different models.
Dialogue: 0,0:38:46.32,0:38:49.44,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, now it's not all just about launching and managing a single model.
Dialogue: 0,0:38:49.49,0:38:53.58,Sub,,0,0,0,,You know, a single query might spawn multiple different models.
Dialogue: 0,0:38:53.63,0:38:58.77,Sub,,0,0,0,,I think what you're seeing is you're seeing the the ratio of CPUs and the growth of CPUs now try to keep up.
Dialogue: 0,0:38:58.82,0:39:02.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,At the end of the day, you're deploying massively expensive infrastructure.
Dialogue: 0,0:39:02.28,0:39:09.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,You're trying to keep that infrastructure operational and drive utilization up as much as possible.
Dialogue: 0,0:39:09.12,0:39:17.16,Sub,,0,0,0,,And uh if the CPUs become the bottleneck, that is the agents can't call uh additional tools,
Dialogue: 0,0:39:17.21,0:39:23.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,can't kind of go manage that flow, you've got idle idle technology there, and that's in nobody's interest.
Dialogue: 0,0:39:23.84,0:39:28.37,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, we know Mohammed that you know, ARM has been in the hyperscale world for a long time.
Dialogue: 0,0:39:28.42,0:39:32.62,Sub,,0,0,0,,AWS using Graviton, Google using Axion, and so on and so forth.
Dialogue: 0,0:39:32.67,0:39:38.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, how do you see enterprises and neo clouds now having access to the AGI CPU?
Dialogue: 0,0:39:38.48,0:39:45.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,What lessons can they learn from the hyperscalers, and how can they adopt these processors to be more efficient in their work on workloads?
Dialogue: 0,0:39:45.12,0:39:51.42,Sub,,0,0,0,,I mean, what you what you saw with the hyperscalers, so so ARM kind of has been in the in the infrastructure or the data center space.
Dialogue: 0,0:39:51.47,0:39:52.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,We started investing in 2011.
Dialogue: 0,0:39:52.96,0:39:56.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, believe it or not, we started investing in the software side in 2011.
Dialogue: 0,0:39:56.76,0:40:02.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,It really started to take off around 2018, 2019 when AWS launched Graviton.
Dialogue: 0,0:40:02.64,0:40:03.30,Sub,,0,0,0,,And at that moment,
Dialogue: 0,0:40:03.35,0:40:08.38,Sub,,0,0,0,,what they did is Graviton had this realization that if they stopped trying to take
Dialogue: 0,0:40:08.43,0:40:15.52,Sub,,0,0,0,,an off-the-shelf uh legacy uh piece of silicon and design their data center around that silicon,
Dialogue: 0,0:40:15.57,0:40:20.56,Sub,,0,0,0,,but rather optimize to the silicon for what they wanted their data center to be,
Dialogue: 0,0:40:20.61,0:40:28.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,they could get massive uh performance and more importantly for them at the time, efficiency improvements.
Dialogue: 0,0:40:28.24,0:40:32.06,Sub,,0,0,0,,That was a kind of watershed moment because really what happened is a lot of the software
Dialogue: 0,0:40:32.11,0:40:37.56,Sub,,0,0,0,,started to kind of move over to ARM and other hyperscalers started to uh to follow suit.
Dialogue: 0,0:40:37.61,0:40:45.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, today you've got Google, you have Microsoft, you have AWS, you have Nvidia, all building based on um based on ARM.
Dialogue: 0,0:40:45.88,0:40:53.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,ARM CPUs and they're doing so because they can optimize those systems for whatever system or architecture they want.
Dialogue: 0,0:40:53.48,0:40:59.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,Because of that, you've got over 10,000 companies around the world today that are using ARM in the cloud every day.
Dialogue: 0,0:40:59.56,0:41:09.86,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's it's that install base which has been effectively limited to cloud-based deployments which ARM AGI CPU now makes available to everybody else.
Dialogue: 0,0:41:09.91,0:41:14.93,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, you can now get all the benefits of that performance, of that efficiency,
Dialogue: 0,0:41:14.98,0:41:18.38,Sub,,0,0,0,,but you can get it on prem or you can leverage it in the cloud either way.
Dialogue: 0,0:41:18.43,0:41:24.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,And I think that's the sort of the sort of watershed or difference in the in in in kind of where we are today.
Dialogue: 0,0:41:24.96,0:41:25.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,Understood.
Dialogue: 0,0:41:25.76,0:41:32.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, when we look at data center infrastructure, we know that the GPUs are getting more power hungry, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:41:32.48,0:41:35.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,Every year they're using more and more power, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:41:35.36,0:41:38.65,Sub,,0,0,0,,ARM has always been, you know, thought of as power efficient.
Dialogue: 0,0:41:38.70,0:41:47.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, how do you see adding more cores, you know, being more and I guess performance optimized while keeping the power efficiency down.
Dialogue: 0,0:41:48.00,0:41:54.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, when we designed ARM AGI CPU, we designed it around three key principles: performance, efficiency, and scale.
Dialogue: 0,0:41:54.20,0:41:56.09,Sub,,0,0,0,,Those were the three things that mattered the most.
Dialogue: 0,0:41:56.14,0:42:02.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,And And if you look at the reality of the world we're living in right now, is we have these massive aspirations for what AI can be.
Dialogue: 0,0:42:02.44,0:42:07.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,We have this massive aspirations for what AGI can get can deliver to us.
Dialogue: 0,0:42:07.08,0:42:09.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh we don't have enough power.
Dialogue: 0,0:42:09.88,0:42:11.02,Sub,,0,0,0,,And we don't have enough compute.
Dialogue: 0,0:42:11.07,0:42:12.22,Sub,,0,0,0,,That's just the reality.
Dialogue: 0,0:42:12.27,0:42:14.46,Sub,,0,0,0,,We just can't build it fast enough.
Dialogue: 0,0:42:14.51,0:42:19.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so, if the world has a fixed footprint of of power,
Dialogue: 0,0:42:19.88,0:42:24.49,Sub,,0,0,0,,and you're trying to put more and more accelerators in there and more and more compute in there,
Dialogue: 0,0:42:24.54,0:42:30.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,then the common denominator, the the thing the only thing that you can affect is to make that system more and more efficient.
Dialogue: 0,0:42:30.48,0:42:35.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,That means holistic system design, a lot of the stuff that that, you know,
Dialogue: 0,0:42:35.20,0:42:40.38,Sub,,0,0,0,,Supermicro works on in terms of making sure that that entire system is efficient when you build it out.
Dialogue: 0,0:42:40.43,0:42:47.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,Oh, but it also means that making sure that you've got the most efficient components in and um down to the silicon level.
Dialogue: 0,0:42:47.76,0:42:54.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,At the system level within ARM, you know, we've been building efficient CPUs and efficient compute for over 35 years.
Dialogue: 0,0:42:54.72,0:43:02.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,Every one of you is carrying around a mobile phone that's effectively a supercomputer in your pocket that works off of a battery.
Dialogue: 0,0:43:02.48,0:43:09.64,Sub,,0,0,0,,We're taking those same design principles and now applying it to the data center so we can cram more compute into that fixed power envelope.
Dialogue: 0,0:43:09.69,0:43:14.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,And at the end of the day, that's at the heart of what of what we do.
Dialogue: 0,0:43:14.60,0:43:21.26,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, when you look at the partnership between ARM and Supermicro, where do you see this partnership helping the Neo Clouds,
Dialogue: 0,0:43:21.31,0:43:25.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,helping the enterprise get to that next level of power efficiency?
Dialogue: 0,0:43:25.28,0:43:27.65,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah, and I've told you and I've told Charles multiple times.
Dialogue: 0,0:43:27.70,0:43:30.25,Sub,,0,0,0,,I mean, I love I love this partnership for a couple of reasons.
Dialogue: 0,0:43:30.30,0:43:36.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,I mean, at the end of the day, we're bringing this kind of, you know, low-power performant efficient compute to the table.
Dialogue: 0,0:43:36.60,0:43:41.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,You know, the reason why we partnered so closely with with Supermicro was was very simple.
Dialogue: 0,0:43:41.60,0:43:44.89,Sub,,0,0,0,,I mean, you guys have this amazing history of execution.
Dialogue: 0,0:43:44.94,0:43:49.89,Sub,,0,0,0,,You have this amazing history of of building out this comprehensive portfolio.
Dialogue: 0,0:43:49.94,0:43:53.13,Sub,,0,0,0,,I mean, you know, I think Charles talked about all of his building blocks.
Dialogue: 0,0:43:53.18,0:43:56.68,Sub,,0,0,0,,I mean, you you see that and it's, you know,
Dialogue: 0,0:43:56.73,0:44:05.66,Sub,,0,0,0,,um as we as we go off and start to kind of make the technology more widely available to a broader group of of customers, two things are clear.
Dialogue: 0,0:44:05.71,0:44:11.73,Sub,,0,0,0,,One, you know, we needed a partner who could go off and execute and get the job done quickly and kind of deliver some amazing,
Dialogue: 0,0:44:11.78,0:44:18.66,Sub,,0,0,0,,you know, amazing products all the way through to to customers who's got that full portfolio that they could kind of bring to bear.
Dialogue: 0,0:44:18.71,0:44:24.58,Sub,,0,0,0,,And I think that combination of the compute that we bring to the table with your history of execution,
Dialogue: 0,0:44:24.64,0:44:30.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,your depth of supply chain and and and your your broad product portfolio kind of
Dialogue: 0,0:44:30.20,0:44:35.53,Sub,,0,0,0,,allows us to serve just an amazing and an all new set of customers for Arm,
Dialogue: 0,0:44:35.58,0:44:36.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,right?
Dialogue: 0,0:44:36.12,0:44:42.78,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, everyone talks about, you know, the AI boom and, you know, how long is it going to be around and how long is this going to happen?
Dialogue: 0,0:44:42.83,0:44:49.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, what are your thoughts on specifically enterprise AI and what you see over the next two to three years?
Dialogue: 0,0:44:49.16,0:44:55.50,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah, I mean, I I guess when I think about enterprise AI and I think about where we are within the AI AI cycle,
Dialogue: 0,0:44:55.55,0:44:58.82,Sub,,0,0,0,,I mean, we are just it's it's really early innings.
Dialogue: 0,0:44:58.87,0:45:00.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,I think that's what's clear.
Dialogue: 0,0:45:00.76,0:45:03.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um, you know, it's been adopted in large scale.
Dialogue: 0,0:45:03.32,0:45:11.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,We're talking about giga gigawatt scale deployments now within, you know, those those massive data centers.
Dialogue: 0,0:45:11.20,0:45:17.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,But the reality is is that compute is going to and and AI is going to be pervasive in everything we do.
Dialogue: 0,0:45:17.08,0:45:20.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's going to be pervasive in our pocket, in our IT cabinet.
Dialogue: 0,0:45:20.24,0:45:24.09,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's going to be pervasive in our automobiles and our robotics.
Dialogue: 0,0:45:24.14,0:45:26.60,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's going to be pervasive kind of end to end.
Dialogue: 0,0:45:26.65,0:45:31.18,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, it isn't just about what we've been focused on, which are just those big data centers.
Dialogue: 0,0:45:31.23,0:45:32.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,Those are going to evolve.
Dialogue: 0,0:45:32.32,0:45:33.41,Sub,,0,0,0,,They're going to have to grow.
Dialogue: 0,0:45:33.46,0:45:35.52,Sub,,0,0,0,,We're going to have to put more and more compute in them.
Dialogue: 0,0:45:35.57,0:45:38.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,We're going to have to get more and more efficient in how we do that.
Dialogue: 0,0:45:38.20,0:45:42.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,But then you need that kind of synergy from there all the way down to those end points.
Dialogue: 0,0:45:42.44,0:45:49.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,I think the future's incredibly exciting because there there is so much potential associated with AI that we just we just haven't realized yet.
Dialogue: 0,0:45:49.32,0:45:53.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,We're we're really just, you know, we're just laying the foundations.
Dialogue: 0,0:45:53.16,0:45:58.10,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um, you know, it's every day there's a new application and a new use case and we're just really scratching the surface.
Dialogue: 0,0:45:58.15,0:46:03.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, I'm really excited to see what happens.
Dialogue: 0,0:46:03.16,0:46:10.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,Okay, as you can see, we already prepared so many architectural with your CPU.
Dialogue: 0,0:46:10.92,0:46:11.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,Absolutely.
Dialogue: 0,0:46:11.64,0:46:20.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,Number one standard system level whatever configuration customer one already.
Dialogue: 0,0:46:20.84,0:46:22.36,Sub,,0,0,0,,This is what I mean, execution.
Dialogue: 0,0:46:22.41,0:46:23.09,Sub,,0,0,0,,Look at this.
Dialogue: 0,0:46:23.14,0:46:31.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,I mean, I we we we kind of showed it to them and and you know, the more than one of these platforms came about because we had a customer and you know,
Dialogue: 0,0:46:31.80,0:46:37.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,I called Charles and Matt up and said, "Hey, we've got this customer they're looking and immediately turned something around.
Dialogue: 0,0:46:37.24,0:46:39.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, I think that's exactly what what I'm talking about.
Dialogue: 0,0:46:39.40,0:46:40.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,No, I need the your chip.
Dialogue: 0,0:46:41.00,0:46:41.69,Sub,,0,0,0,,We're ready.
Dialogue: 0,0:46:41.74,0:46:42.26,Sub,,0,0,0,,Let's go.
Dialogue: 0,0:46:42.31,0:46:42.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,Let's go.
Dialogue: 0,0:46:42.88,0:46:43.57,Sub,,0,0,0,,Absolutely.
Dialogue: 0,0:46:43.62,0:46:44.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,Absolutely.
Dialogue: 0,0:46:44.36,0:46:45.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, it should be very soon, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:46:45.92,0:46:49.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah, we we're going to be in production within within a few months here.
Dialogue: 0,0:46:49.76,0:46:51.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, we're really excited about it.
Dialogue: 0,0:46:51.36,0:46:52.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,Really excited about it.
Dialogue: 0,0:46:52.60,0:46:53.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,Good.
Dialogue: 0,0:46:53.16,0:46:57.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, for customer here we are ready to take order.
Dialogue: 0,0:46:57.68,0:46:58.74,Sub,,0,0,0,,Absolutely.
Dialogue: 0,0:46:58.79,0:46:59.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,Bring it on.
Dialogue: 0,0:47:00.00,0:47:00.40,Sub,,0,0,0,,Thank you.
